# File: tests/features/add_greeting_digit_count_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/227-add-greeting-digit-count-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Count ASCII digits in the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Count ASCII digits in the completed greeting
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_digit_count is called with R2D2, Agent 007, and Ada
    Then the results are the Python int values 2, 3, and 0

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Count only the ten ASCII digits
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_digit_count is called with fullwidth U+FF11 U+FF12, Arabic-Indic U+0663, and x with superscript U+00B2
    Then the results are 0, 0, and 0

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_digit_count is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_digit_count of R2D2
    Then it prints 2 and greeting_digit_count is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the ASCII 0-9 set, completed-greeting scope, and inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0
